# SQL fixtures are compiled in with `include_str!`, which embeds the file bytes
# unchanged -- unlike a Rust string literal, where the compiler normalizes CRLF.
# Several fixtures are executed as DDL and then read back out of `sqlite_schema`,
# where SQLite stores the statement text verbatim, and both the byte-exact schema
# guard and the v12 trigger reconstruction compare that text against LF-only
# separators. With `core.autocrlf=true` a fresh clone rewrites these files to CRLF
# and those comparisons fail, which is invisible in a working copy that was written
# rather than checked out. Pin the checkout instead of teaching every consumer to
# accept both.
*.sql text eol=lf
